Z||000000||batboy||06-19-99||08:47 PM||||My speedometer only works every once in a while. When it doesn't work, the needle just stops (it's at 45 mph right now). I've tested the speed sensor and it works fine. I have two Fieros, so I switched sensors, but still no joy. My question is this, I suppose it's time now for me to tear out the dash and remove the speedo. Short of taking the one I know works out of the other car and swapping them, is there a quick and easy method of bench testing a Fiero speedometer (I don't want to disassemble two dashes). If it's bad, I'd rather replace it with a 120 mph speedo, I might even put an aftermarket one in such as a VDO. If the gauge checks out ok, then I assume it must be a short in the wiring, right? There were a couple of ground wires diconnected in the engine compartment, but I have those fixed now. I suppose there are grounds up under the dash too, right? But why would the speedo be stuck at 45 mph if it was a wiring problem? I suspect the speedo itself has gone south. Any ideas?
